From 0b674e29eef70f70362afbe86b7ab36c7ca473ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarthSlops <justin.duverge@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:58:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ops): publish immutable sha- image tags; time-scope the
 deploy prune
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Applies the fix O2's documentation half recommended, with founder
approval — deployment workflow changes are founder-gated.

deploy.yml published only :main, overwritten every deploy, so "redeploy
the previous tag" named nothing. The deploy step then ran a bare
docker image prune -f right after pull + up -d, deleting the image it had
just replaced — destroying the only local artifact a rollback could have
used, moments after creating the need for one. Rollback by GHCR digest
still worked, but nothing recorded digests and reading them needs
read:packages, so recovery depended on a value nobody wrote down, found
mid-outage through a UI.

Both images now also publish :sha-<commit>, immutable and readable off the
commit history, and the prune is scoped to --filter "until=168h" so a
week of previous builds survives as a local fallback.

Rollback drops from a digest hunt to a tag change. The runbook is updated
to the new path and keeps the digest procedure as a documented fallback
for builds pushed before today, which carry no sha- tag — along with the
before/after account, so a later "cleanup" that trims the tag list back to
one entry can see what that costs.

Backend 570/570 — no application code touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/deploy.yml | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
index 8fb7a41..c923b47 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
@@ -111,6 +111,7 @@ jobs:
           push: true
           tags: |
             ghcr.io/justinduverge-design/omen:main
+            ghcr.io/justinduverge-design/omen:sha-${{ github.sha }}
           cache-from: type=gha,scope=omen-api
           cache-to: type=gha,mode=max,scope=omen-api
           build-args: |
@@ -128,6 +129,7 @@ jobs:
           push: true
           tags: |
             ghcr.io/justinduverge-design/omen-cron:main
+            ghcr.io/justinduverge-design/omen-cron:sha-${{ github.sha }}
           cache-from: type=gha,scope=omen-cron
           cache-to: type=gha,mode=max,scope=omen-cron
 
@@ -155,8 +157,13 @@ jobs:
           docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml --project-name omen pull api cron
           echo '==> Recreating API and cron containers (env_file: .env.production stays on KVM1)'
           docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml --project-name omen up -d --no-build api cron
-          echo '==> Cleaning up dangling images'
-          docker image prune -f
+          echo '==> Cleaning up dangling images older than 7 days'
+          # Time-scoped on purpose (O2). A bare `docker image prune -f` removed the image
+          # this deploy had just replaced — deleting the only local artifact a rollback
+          # could have used, moments after creating the need for one. 168h keeps a week of
+          # previous builds on disk as a fallback while still bounding growth.
+          docker image prune -f --filter "until=168h"
+
 
       - name: Smoke test /api/health (retries up to 60s)
         run: |
-- 
